<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Werla</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Werla was a royal palace (Pfalz) of the Ottonian kings on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oker">Oker</a> river near Schladen in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-fowler">Henry the Fowler</a> took refuge there from a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyar</a> raid in 926 before agreeing a nine-year truce, and Otto I and his successors held assemblies there. It declined after the Salian kings favoured nearby Goslar, and excavations have uncovered its walls and buildings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/werla.jpg" alt="Werla" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Okernick · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WerlaWestturmVonSueden.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
